      "source_path": ".jules/sentinel.md",
      "line": 2,
      "text": "**Vulnerability:** The Next.js application lacked global security headers, making it vulnerable to clickjacking, MIME-type sniffing, and missing HTTPS enforcement."
    },
    {
      "kind": "security",
      "source_path": ".jules/sentinel.md",
      "line": 3,
      "text": "**Learning:** Next.js requires manual configuration of security headers via the `headers()` function in `next.config.mjs`. Without this, applications are deployed without standard HTTP protections."
    },
    {
      "kind": "security",
      "source_path": ".jules/sentinel.md",
      "line": 4,
      "text": "**Prevention:** Always configure `X-Frame-Options`, `X-Content-Type-Options`, `Referrer-Policy`, `Permissions-Policy`, and `Strict-Transport-Security` headers globally in the `next.config.mjs` file for all new Next.js projects."
